Clove Notch, later widened to standard gauge; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1882, "end": 1893, "headway_min": 480, "note": "The Stony Clove and Catskill Mountain Railroad was organized January 18 1881 as a 3-foot narrow-gauge line connecting with the Ulster and Delaware at Phoenicia. Construction was delayed by labor shortages; by August 1881 the line reached Edgewood (8.5 miles from Phoenicia), and it opened through the Stony Clove Notch to Hunter on June 24 1882. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulster_and_Delaware_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gettysburg_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_Mountain_Railroad", "https://durr.org/about/", "https://www.dailygazette.com/hv360/opinion/columnists/the-stony-clove-catskill-mountain-and-kaaterskill-railroads/", "search results citing full mainline station list: Shandaken, Big Indian, Grand Hotel, Fleischmanns, Arkville, Kellys Cor\u2026"]}, {"start": 1893, "end": 1932, "headway_min": 300, "note": "The Ulster and Delaware Railroad Company acquired control of the Stony Clove and Catskill Mountain Railroad (and the connecting Kaaterskill Railroad) on June 4 1893. The line was later widened from narrow to standard gauge. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulster_and_Delaware_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gettysburg_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_Mountain_Railroad", "https://durr.org/ab