d Tannersville Junction) connected there with the separate, standard-gauge Kaaterskill Railroad for onward travel to Tannersville and the Catskill Mountain House resort district. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulster_and_Delaware_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gettysburg_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_Mountain_Railroad", "https://durr.org/about/", "https://www.dailygazette.com/hv360/opinion/columnists/the-stony-clove-catskill-mountain-and-kaaterskill-railroads/", "search results citing full mainline station list: Shandaken, Big Indian, Grand Hotel, Fleischmanns, Arkville, Kellys Cor\u2026"]}, {"start": 1893, "end": 1899, "headway_min": 300, "note": "The Ulster and Delaware acquired control of both the Stony Clove and Catskill Mountain Railroad and the Kaaterskill Railroad on June 4 1893. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulster_and_Delaware_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gettysburg_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_Mountain_Railroad", "https://durr.org/about/", "https://www.dailygazette.com/hv360/opinion/columnists/the-stony-clove-catskill-mountain-and-kaaterskill-railroads/", "search results citing full mainline station list: Shandaken, Big Indian, Grand Hotel, Fleischmanns, Arkville, Kellys Cor\u2026"]}, {"start": 1899, "end": 1932, "headway_min": 240, "note": "The Ulster and Delaware converted the Kaaterskill Railroad to standard gauge (4ft 8.5in) in 1899, integrating it fully with the rest of the U&D system. This branch ran parallel to (and competed with) the separately-owned, narrow-gauge Catskill and Tannersville Railway, which went bankrupt in 1918 and was scrapped in 1919. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ulster_and_Delaware_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gettysburg_Railroad", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catskill_Mountain_Railroad", "https://durr.org/about/", "https://www.dailygazette.com/hv360/opinion/columnists/the-stony-clove-catskill-mountain-and-kaaterskill-railroads/", "search results citing full mainline station list: Shandaken, Big Indian, Grand Hotel, Fleischmanns, Arkville, Kellys Cor\u2026"]}]}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-74.21237, 42.14037], [-74.20139, 42.16527], [-74.21149, 42.14013], [-74.21184, 42.14172], [-74.21188, 42.14228], [-74.21185, 42.14289], [-74.21143, 42.14352], [-74.21037, 42.14484], [-74.20954, 42.14536], [-74.20905, 42.14604], [-74.20872, 42.14687], [-74.20871, 42.14782], [-74.20855, 42.14874], [-74.20801, 42.14951], [-74.20711, 42.15024], [-74.20642, 42.15105], [-74.2054, 42.15292], [-74.20489, 42.15376], [-74.20412, 42.15534], [-74.20401, 42.15608], [-74.2041, 42.15667], [-74.20436, 42.15727], [-74.20432, 42.15801], [-74.20383, 42.15863], [-74.20324, 42.15915], [-74.20271, 42.15954], [-74.20236, 42.16012], [-74.20211, 42.16084], [-74.2019, 42.16163], [-74.20177, 42.16247], [-74.20116, 42.16508], [-74.20081, 42.16587], [-74.20056, 42.16679], [-74.19991, 42.16862], [-74.19943, 42.16963], [-74.19874, 42.1705], [-74.1981, 42.17153], [-74.19753, 42.17262], [-74.19705, 42.17384], [-74.19637, 42.17632], [-74.19597, 42.17751],